  "lineage": "Night-time Minangkabau entertainment of West Sumatra in which singers trade dendang, sung pantun verses often melancholy in tone, accompanied by the saluang, an end-blown bamboo flute open at both ends and played with circular breathing (here the credited bamboo-flute card). Performances run through the night at weddings and village gatherings; the related dendang Pauah comes from Pauh in Padang.",
